< InvisiSpec_6 -- footprint model for InvisiSpec (Yan et al., MICRO 2018), branch (control-flow) speculation.
< Copy of STT_6.als (2026-11-09, new file requested by Anna). Differences are confined
< to the "Specific defense model" block at the bottom: two clause lines change (the
< leakage function and the protection-set propagation); everything else is
< byte-identical to STT_6.als.
<   - protection set = ALL memory, never untainted (STT_6 untaints a location once a
<     load with no older unresolved branch reads it). A test exists when a speculative
<     load's address derives from a memory value, wherever that value was read.
<   - transmitters = load addresses only (STT_6 also has branch conditions).
<   - speculation contract = STT_6's (after an unresolved branch).
< The defense block is the same in InvisiSpec_6, CleanupSpec_6 and SpecLFB_6: the three
< papers make the same promise about a speculative load. Store-bypass speculation is
< in InvisiSpec_6_stl.als. See wiki/design/MODELS_AND_BUILDS.md PART 8.
